<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8" standalone="yes"?><rss version="2.0" xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><channel><title>Ezurio on Tech Insights: AI &amp; Cloud</title><link>https://shoubhikbanerjee.github.io/blog/tags/ezurio/</link><description>Recent content in Ezurio on Tech Insights: AI &amp; Cloud</description><generator>Hugo -- gohugo.io</generator><language>en-us</language><lastBuildDate>Sat, 05 Sep 2026 22:02:16 +0530</lastBuildDate><atom:link href="https://shoubhikbanerjee.github.io/blog/tags/ezurio/index.xml" rel="self" type="application/rss+xml"/><item><title>Ezurio Releases Tiny OSM-MF Module Featuring Linux Support and AI Capabilities</title><link>https://shoubhikbanerjee.github.io/blog/p/ezurio-releases-tiny-osm-mf-module-featuring-linux-support-and-ai-capabilities/</link><pubDate>Sat, 05 Sep 2026 22:02:16 +0530</pubDate><guid>https://shoubhikbanerjee.github.io/blog/p/ezurio-releases-tiny-osm-mf-module-featuring-linux-support-and-ai-capabilities/</guid><description>&lt;h1 id="ezurio-releases-tiny-osm-mf-module-featuring-linux-support-and-ai-capabilities"&gt;Ezurio Releases Tiny OSM-MF Module Featuring Linux Support and AI Capabilities
&lt;/h1&gt;&lt;p&gt;Ezurio has introduced the Tiny OSM-MF module, a hardware component designed to run Linux on the Sitara AM67 processor with integrated 4-TOPS AI performance.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2 id="-key-details"&gt;⚙️ Key details
&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;The module is built for the Cortex-A53 cores and supports a variety of operating systems. Ezurio provides software support for the following environments:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;table&gt;
&lt;thead&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;th style="text-align: left"&gt;Operating System&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;th style="text-align: left"&gt;Support Status&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;/thead&gt;
&lt;tbody&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td style="text-align: left"&gt;Yocto Linux&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td style="text-align: left"&gt;Supported&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td style="text-align: left"&gt;Buildroot Linux&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td style="text-align: left"&gt;Supported&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td style="text-align: left"&gt;Android&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td style="text-align: left"&gt;Supported&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td style="text-align: left"&gt;Debian&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td style="text-align: left"&gt;Supported&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td style="text-align: left"&gt;QNX&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td style="text-align: left"&gt;Supported&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;/tbody&gt;
&lt;/table&gt;
&lt;p&gt;#Ezurio #Linux #Hardware #AI&lt;/p&gt;
